    <bpmn:process id="W_W4600" name="W4600. Circular-Economy Impact, ESG Reporting &amp; Program Review" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: ESG cycle (VS-25); program review
Frequency: Quarterly + annual
Volume: Circular-economy impact &amp; ESG reporting for the program
Owner: ESG (VS-25) / Circular Lead / Merchandising
Participants: Finance (VS-17.4), Sustainability (VS-25.2), Strategy (VS-33), Board (VS-36)
Source: workflow W4600 — Circular-Economy Impact, ESG Reporting &amp; Program Review</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4600_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4600_Lane1" name="ESG">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4600_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4600_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4600_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4600_Lane2" name="Strategy">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4600_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4600_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4600_Start4" name="ESG cycle (VS-25); program review">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4600_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4600_Task5" name="ESG/Circular quantify circular-economy impact (units refurbished/resold, waste…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: ESG/Circular quantify circular-economy impact (units refurbished/resold, waste diverted W4590, material recovered, CO2e avoided vs new-manufacture), aligned to VS-25/VS-73
Responsible (R): ESG / Circular / Data
Accountable (A): ESG Lead / CSO
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4600_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4600_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4600_Task6" name="ESG/Sustainability report the impact in ESG/sustainability disclosure…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: ESG/Sustainability report the impact in ESG/sustainability disclosure (VS-25/GRI/W4523), with data traceability (VS-21), avoiding overstatement (greenwashing VS-152/W4527)
Responsible (R): ESG / Sustainability / Audit
Accountable (A): CSO / CFO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4600_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4600_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4600_Task7" name="Strategy/Merchandising/Circular review the program (circular + economic…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Strategy/Merchandising/Circular review the program (circular + economic performance W4599), and decide scale/adjust/exit per strategy (VS-33), board-reported (VS-36)
Responsible (R): Strategy / Merchandising / Circular
Accountable (A): VP Merch / Board
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4600_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4600_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4600_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4600_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4600_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-697 (ensure controlled execution — Resale Listing, Fulfillment, Warranty &amp; Analytics (PA-155.3).) | - CTL-697: circular impact conservatively measured &amp; traceable (VS-21); greenwashing-controlled (W4527); program reviewed on dual circular+economic metrics (W4599)
Owner: ESG (VS-25) / Circular Lead / Merchandising</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
